  "raw_text": "134\n\nLankira\n \n(adj)\n \n–\n \nlearned, skilled, qualified, experienced\n \n(describing\n \na person who has learned or who has\n\nexperience\n) / aprendido, capacitado, calificado, experimentado (describiendo a una persona que ha aprendido\n\no que tiene experiencia)\n\n(Ex/Ej\n(\nmwb\n-\n08/20\n):\n \nJetró bui Moses ra win wark kum kum dauki kan ba waitna lankira nani ra laki yabaia\n \n–\n \nJethro told\n\nMoses to hand over (to delegate) some of the work he was doing to qualified men\n \n/ Jetro le dijo a Moisés que entregara\n\n(delegar) parte del trabajo que estaba haciendo a hombres calificados)\n\nSmalki tataukra lankira\n \n–\n \nexperienced publisher\n \n/ publicador experimentado\n\nSmasmalkra lankira\n \n–\n \nexperienced teacher/preacher\n \n/\n \nprofesor\n/predicador experimentado\n\nWark tatakra lankira\n \n–\n \nexperienced worker, skilled worker\n \n/ trabajador experimentado, trabajador calificado\n\nLangkaia\n \n(a/t:\n \nWlangkaia\n)\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto swallow, to absorb, to gulp, to engulf, to devour, to hang, to strangle, to choke, to\nstifle\n \n/ tragar, absorber, engullir, devorar, colgar, estrangular, ahogar, sofocar\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nlfb54\n):\n \nJehova inska tarka tara kum blikan Jona ra langkaia\n \n–\n \nJehovah sent an enormous fish to swallow Jonah\n \n/ Jehová\nenvió un pez enorme para tragarse a Jonás)\n\nBîla kwâki langkaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto swallow with an open mouth, to gulp with an open mouth\n \n/ tragar con la boca abierta\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nmwb-12/19\n):\n \nTasba ba ai bîla kwâki awalka langkan\n \n–\n \nThe earth swallowed up the river\n \n/ La tierra se tragó el río)\n\nLangni\n \n(adj,n/s)\n \n–\n \neven, level, plain\n \n/ par, llano\n\n(Construct:\n \nLangnika\n)\n\nTwi langni\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nplain\n \n/ llano\n\nLangsa\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nspear, lance\n \n/ lanza\n\nLanhkaia\n \n(\ndb,dictu\n;\n \nLangkaia\n-dba,my,lrw\n;\n \nLahnkaia\n-dbta\n;\n \nLahngkaia\n-dict\n) (v-trans; intrans:\n \nLanhwaia\n)\n \n–\n \nto untie, to\nloosen, to untangle, to release\n \n/ desatar, soltar, desenredar\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nlfb57\n):\n \nPashur yauhkika titan ra lanhkan\n \n–\nThe next day in the morning, Pashur released (Jeremiah)\n \n/ Al día siguiente en la\nmañana, Pashur liberado (Jeremías))\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nlfb73\n):\n \nAi sûska awa nani lanhkaia sin sip apia sna\n \n–\n \nI am not able to untie his shoe laces\n \n/ No puedo desatar sus cordones)\n\nLanhwaia\n \n(v-intrans; trans:\n \nLanhkaia\n)\n \n–\n \nto untie, to loosen, to untangle, to release\n \n/ desatar, soltar, desenredar\n\nLap tikaia\n \n(a/t:\n \nLap-tikaia\n-dict\n;\n \nLaptikaia\n-sp\n) (v-trans; intrans:\n \nLap tiwaia\n)\n \n–\n \nto lose suddenly\n \n/ perder de repente\n\nLap tiwaia\n \n(a/t:\n \nLap-tiwaia\n-\ndict\n;\n \nLaptiwaia\n-sp\n) (v-intrans; trans:\n \nLap tikaia\n)\n \n–\n \nto be lost suddenly, to vanish, to disappear\n\n/ perderse de repente, desaparecer\n\nLapaskaia\n \n–\n \nsee/ver:\n \nLapatkaia\n\nLapaswaia\n \n–\n \nsee/ver:\n \nLapatwaia\n\nLapatkaia\n \n(a/t:\n \nLapaskaia\n) (v-trans; intrans:\n \nLapatwaia\n)\n \n–\n \nto bend, to twist, to shrink, to flatten, to smash, to dent\n \n/\ndoblar, torcer, encoger, aplanar, aplastar, abollar\n\nLapatwaia\n \n(a/t:\n \nLapaswaia\n) (v-intrans; trans:\n \nLapatkaia\n)\n \n–\n \nto be bent, to be twisted, to be shrunken, to be flattened, to\nbe smashed, to be dented\n \n/ doblarse, torcerse, encogerse, aplastarse, abollarse\n\nLapatwanka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nbend, twist, dent\n \n/ doblar, torcer, abollar\n\nLapta\n \n(adj)\n \n–\n \nhot\n \n(usually referring to the heat from the sun) / caliente (generalmente se refiere al calor del sol)\n\nLapta daukaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto heat, to warm\n \n/ calentar\n\nLapta ingnika\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nsunlight\n \n/ luz del sol\n\nLapta takaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto grow hot\n \n(often referring to the day becoming hotter) / calentarse (a menudo refiriéndose a\nque el día se calienta más)\n\nUba lapta sa\n \n(exp)\n \n–\n \nThe sun is hot\n\nLapta\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nsun\n \n/ sol\n\nLapta aihlakaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto get a sunburn\n \n/ tener una quemadura de sol\n\nLaptika\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nheat, sweat, zeal, excitement, enthusiasm, fervor, passion, eagerness\n \n/ calor, sudor, celo, entusiasmo,\nfervor, pasión\n\nLaptika sakaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto sweat\n \n/ sudar\n\nLaptika takaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto sweat, to perspire\n \n/ sudar, transpirar\n\nLâs\n \n(Las)\n \n(adv,adj)\n \n–\n \nlast\n, latest\n, final\n \n/ último\n, final\n\nLâs kat, ...\n \n–\n \nat the last point, ..., finally, ...\n \n/ en el último punto, ..., finalmente, ...\n\nLâs ra, ...\n \n–\n \nat the last, ..., in the end, ..., finally, ...\n \n/ al final, ..., finalmente, ...\n\nL\nâ\ns yua nani\n \n–\n \nlast days\n \n/ últimos días\n \n(Alt:\n \nTnata yua nani\n)\n\n(\nEx/Ej:\n \nYawan l\nâ\ns piua nani ra iwisa ki?\n \n–\n \nAre we living in the last days?\n \n/ ¿Estamos viviendo en los últimos días?\n)",
